                   M I C R O G R O O V E
      analog vinyl, diamond & tube signal path in 8 kilobytes
                    an 8k intro by Latent

  ------------------------------------------------------------

      type ........ 8k intro
      platform .... Windows, browser (WebGL2)
      size ........ 8,187 bytes, one HTML file (5 bytes free)
      length ...... 2:02.88 (64 bars @ 125 BPM, 1.92 s/bar)
      tempo ....... 125 BPM, F Dorian / F Minor (Picardy Fmaj9)
      released .... November 2026
      group ....... Latent

  ------------------------------------------------------------
    credits
  ------------------------------------------------------------

      code ........ Gemini 4 Carbon
      graphics .... Gemini 4 Carbon
      music ....... Gemini 4 Carbon
      harness ..... Antigravity

      Gemini 4 Carbon is an AI model made by Google DeepMind.
      It designed the concept and wrote the shaders, loader
      and soundtrack. It inspected rendered frames, contact
      sheets, loudness/RMS stats, and spectral band metrics,
      but could not hear the music or watch it run in real time.

  ------------------------------------------------------------
    the programme
  ------------------------------------------------------------

      0:00  I   33 1/3 RPM       turntable plinth, chrome strobe
                                 turret & dots, diamond drop at bar 4
      0:15  II  45/45 STEREO     curved obsidian stereo V-groove
                                 canyon & octahedral carbon stylus
      0:42  III CLASS A          twin vacuum tubes: 2400K tungsten
                                 heaters, cobalt-violet plasma & VU
      1:01  IV  ANTI-SKATE       power-brake drop, floating bokeh
                                 crystals & spin-up snare build
      1:16  V   45 RPM           overdrive canyon, 45 RPM rainbow
                                 spectrum LP, glowing tubes & VU push
      1:47  VI  LOCKED GROOVE    Picardy Fmaj9 run-out, cue-lift of
                                 diamond off vinyl mirror, credits

  ------------------------------------------------------------
    how to run
  ------------------------------------------------------------

      Double-click intro.html in Edge or Chrome on Windows 10
      or 11, wait for "CLICK" (~4.4 s while shaders compile and
      the soundtrack renders), then click for fullscreen.
      No server, no browser flags. ESC exits fullscreen. A
      discrete GPU is expected. Tested on Edge with an RTX
      5090 (2.1-5.9 ms/frame at 1080p).

  ------------------------------------------------------------
    inside
  ------------------------------------------------------------

      Four raymarched stages (turntable, 45/45 stereo canyon,
      Class-A vacuum tube preamp, dual backlit analog VU
      meters) share a unified 2-bounce raymarcher, 9-step
      adaptive shadow+AO loop, and a 4096x1 RGBA16F groove &
      ballistic VU texture downsampled directly from the
      synthesised AudioBuffer so canyon walls, tube plasma,
      45 RPM LP ridges, and meter needles lock 1:1 to audio.

      Soundtrack runs at 48 kHz into a 4096x1440 RGBA32F
      texture (5,898,240 samples): Rhodes FM electric piano,
      resonant saw chord pad, FM clavinet 16th chops, octave
      slap funk bass, kick/clap/16th hats/crashes, resonant
      portamento lead hooks, needle-drop thump & turntable
      brake, processed through a 4-line Householder FDN with
      17,280-sample dotted-eighth echo and tanh bus limiter.

